# PSScriptAnalyzer analysis scope for this repository (#571 / #578).
#
# Purpose: the PowerShell arm of Gate 1 analyses PRODUCT code. Without this file
# the adapter falls back to a whole-repo scan, which sweeps in interactive
# installer scripts -- `setup-dsh.ps1` exists to print progress to a human, so it
# uses Write-Host by design and trips PSAvoidUsingWriteHost repeatedly. Gating it
# against product rules either blocks every PowerShell-touching commit or forces
# the rule set open, and both outcomes end with PowerShell not being gated at all.
#
# Rules that apply here are declared in PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1, which the
# adapter REQUIRES alongside this file: a scope without a declared rule set would
# silently grade against defaults, so the run is refused (fail-closed) instead.
#
# Every path listed must exist. A missing entry means product code escaped the
# gate (renamed, moved, or added without updating this file) and is reported as
# a WARN inside the scoring denominator -- not silently analysed less.

# Product code: the shared complexity measurement used by the gate suite.
githooks/lib/Measure-PowerShellComplexity.ps1

# NOT listed, deliberately:
#   plugins/dsh/setup-dsh.ps1 (+ its src/npm-package mirror)
#     Interactive environment-setup script. Write-Host is its interface to the
#     operator, not a defect. Kept out of product scope rather than suppressed
#     line by line, so a real rule violation elsewhere in it cannot hide behind
#     a suppression block.
